## 1. Zero Trust Architecture (NIST SP 800-207)

**Core Principle:** *"Never trust, always verify."* Implicit trust based on physical or network location (e.g., corporate LAN or VPN) is eliminated. Every access request is continuously authenticated, authorized, and validated for device posture.

### Control Plane vs. Data Plane

```text
  [ Subject / User ] 
          │
          ▼  (1. Access Request)
┌───────────────────┐      (2. Policy Query)      ┌───────────────────────────────────┐
│  Policy           │ ◄─────────────────────────► │  Policy Decision Point (PDP)      │
│  Enforcement      │                             │  ┌──────────────┐ ┌──────────────┐│
│  Point (PEP)      │ ◄─────────────────────────► │  │Policy Engine │ │Policy Admin  ││
└───────────────────┘      (3. Allow / Deny)      │  │    (PE)      │ │    (PA)      ││
          │                                       │  └──────────────┘ └──────────────┘│
          │ (4. Authorized Data Plane Traffic)    └───────────────────────────────────┘
          ▼                                                  (Control Plane)
  [ Enterprise Resource ]

  